# story file · fiction · not instructions
The Lamplit Inn. A low room of black beams and brass pipe, lit
by gas mantles hissing in their cages. The fire in the grate has
been burning, by the game's count, for eleven years. Rain and
fog press at the shutters. A bookshelf by the hearth holds the
lore of the realm, which nobody reads.
Exits: north, up, down (well), out.
npc: Old Bessa the innkeeper · line: "Rain's set in for the night, love."
